From: Sobs <antohasobne@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] rmg: passable maps, natural obstacles, map check

Random maps could have parts no hero gets to: a main town whose gate
stands in water or in a pocket sealed by water and obstacles, objects
behind obstacles or under underground rock, guards inside rocks,
sealed pockets of land, and template connections that exist only on
paper (a "connection by water" over a lake too small to get boats, or
a lake where no boat fitted).

Checked on the finished map (lib/rmg/RmgValidator): the real objects
and terrain, walking, boats and shipyards, monoliths and subterranean
gates; guards count as passable, they are there to be fought. From
every player's town all other players, zones, template connections
(only through the two zones, or by sea) and visitable objects must be
reachable, and no land may be sealed off. What fails is repaired:
- obstacles (or rock underground) on the cheapest way in are cleared,
  only inside the zone of the target so no zone guard is bypassed, the
  way 2-3 tiles wide, and the cleared ground gets obstacles again
  around it; two water tiles at most become a land bridge;
- a broken connection gets a way through the obstacles between the
  zones with the template's guard at the border, else a boat on the
  shared sea, else a pair of monoliths placed in obstacles far from
  other objects, its entrance guarded;
- land objects in water or on rock get land under them, obstacles
  over an entrance go, sealed pockets get obstacles (big ones are
  opened instead), empty one-tile spurs are planted over.
A map that still fails is generated again (3 attempts at most).

At the source:
- the main town was moved by (2, 2) after its place had been checked,
  into water or out of the zone: the gate is now aimed at the zone's
  centre while the place is searched;
- a connection counts as made by water only over a lake big enough to
  get boats;
- a required object that does not fit no longer drops all the
  required objects after it (the other end of a monolith pair, mines);
- a wide connection is several passages along the common border, not
  one gap.

Landscape (lib/rmg/modificators/ObstaclePlacer): mountains only form
ridges along a zone's edge or the heart of a wide blocked mass, not a
wall in the middle of open land; mountains, forests and lakes grow next
to their own kind, forests rather inside the zone; the tiles along
roads stay open. ObstacleProxy keeps each obstacle's kind from its
biome set and asks the placer how much an obstacle is wanted at a place.

Measured on the host over 428 maps (107 VCMI and HotA templates x 4
seeds, smallest size), checked independently of the generator: maps with
unreachable objects 45 -> 0, with players cut off from each other
70 -> 0, with sealed land 331 -> 0 (not counted: [HotA] Boomerang, whose
zone 11 the template connects to nothing); 11 maps needed a second
attempt; time per map +14%. Largest sizes: 107 maps, all clean, one
second attempt. On the ODROID-GO Advance the check takes 0.15 s on a
72x72 map and 2.6 s of 37 s on a 144x144 two-level map for 8 players.
